    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1126">

                <pb facs="1044" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/2122</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">J. Nr. A 3090]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 4</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: It is reported in the
                    press that English officers are supervising the manufacture of arms and
                    ammunition ordered in this country by Great Britain in the factories here, the
                    works of the Bethlehem Steel Company among others.</p>
                <p>I should be thankful to your excellency if you would kindly ascertain and inform
                    me whether this press report is true.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
